# .trivyignore — CVEs exempt from the Trivy image gate (ci.yml docker-image job
# and publish.yml). One CVE or GHSA ID per line.
#
# Every entry must state what it is, why it cannot be fixed, and the condition
# that removes it again — the same rule as scripts/audit-allowlist.sh. An entry
# here is a security gate held open; keep this list as short as it can be.
#
# An entry may only waive an advisory scripts/audit-allowlist.sh also waives (by
# its GHSA or CVE id), so it retires with that waiver; scripts/waiver-check.mjs
# enforces this.
#
# Unfixed CVEs need no entry: the gate runs with ignore-unfixed, because there is
# nothing to upgrade to. Only a *fixable* finding that genuinely cannot take the
# fix belongs here.

# CVE-2026-118664 (GHSA-qr28-fpjm-wq7f) — decode-uri-component denial of service
# via quadratic decoding of percent-encoded input.
#   WHY: the same advisory is waived for the lockfile gates in
#   scripts/audit-allowlist.sh, which says why minio's query-string@7 cannot take
#   the ESM-only 0.5.1 and why the vulnerable decoder is never reached.
#   REMOVE WHEN: scripts/waiver-check.mjs reports it — it fails CI and the weekly
#   waiver review as soon as a fix is reachable or the advisory no longer applies.
CVE-2026-118664
